    "title": "The Bruins are heading to the NHL Playoffs. Here's when the puck drops",
    "text": "April 15, 2026, 10:09 a.m. ETThe Boston Bruins are heading to the NHL Playoffs after missing them last year.The Bruins will play the Buffalo Sabres in the first round of the NHL Playoffs.If the Bruins defeat the Sabres in the upcoming series, the team would advance to face the winner of the series between the Florida Panthers and the New York Rangers.It's true − the Boston Bruins are heading to the playoffs.The Bruins secured the number-one wild card spot in the NHL's Eastern Conference after defeating the New Jersey Devils 4-0 on Monday at TD Garden in Boston.That should come to the relief of many fans, as the Bruins missed the playoffs in 2025.The Bruins finished this season with a record of 45-27-10, fourth place in the NHL's Atlantic Division.When do the NHL Playoffs begin, and who will the Bruins be playing?Here's what to know.When do the NHL Playoffs begin for the Bruins?The NHL Playoffs begin April 18, 2026. The league has not yet announced the exact day that the Bruins-Sabres series will begin.How many games in the Bruins-Sabres series?There are seven games in the upcoming series.What time does the first Bruins-Sabres playoff game start?That has not been determined yet.Where is the first game in the series being played?The first two games in the series will be at the KeyBank Center in Buffalo, NY, the home ice of the Sabres. Games three and four will be at TD Garden in Boston.How to watch the Bruins against the SabresYou can watch the game locally on NESN, or you can stream the game on ESPN+. Fans can also stream the game on FuboTV or NESN 360.Stream the game!The game will air nationally on truTV and TNT.People can listen to the game on 98.5 the Sports Hub, or via the station's app.Who would the Bruins play if they beat the Sabres in this series?If the Bruins defeat the Sabres in the upcoming series, the team would advance to face the winner of the series between the Florida Panthers and the New York Rangers, who are facing each other in the first round of the playoffs.Our editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, however our editorial decisions remain independent. If you buy through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices and availability may change.",
